# Force LF on every generated corpus artifact, so their bytes are platform-stable for
# each consumer that byte-hashes them. With core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes,
# checkout re-materializes CRLF and a raw hash reports a difference that isn't one
# (Unpopped's git-hash-object note). The freshness gates are BYTE compares, so these
# files must be LF on disk on every platform.
#
# The scope was one file — the structure_key byte-match reference — because a
# corpus-wide renormalization was expected to carry a large one-time diff that would
# collide with an open freshness-gate PR. Measured under #162, that diff DOES NOT
# EXIST: the committed blobs are already LF, so the CRLF is a working-tree
# materialization only, and `git add --renormalize conformance/corpus` stages nothing.
# The narrow scope was avoiding a cost that was never going to be paid, so the rule now
# covers what it always should have — the whole generated corpus, not one file of it.
conformance/corpus/*.json text eol=lf
